## 3. HOW TO INVOKE THE AGENT AND GET RESPONSES

### Basic Flow:

```csharp
// 1. Create IChatClient from OpenAI (from Microsoft.Extensions.AI.OpenAI)
var client = new OpenAI.OpenAIClient(apiKey);
var chatClient = client.AsChatClient(modelId: "gpt-4");

// 2. Create ChatClientAgent
var agent = new ChatClientAgent(
    chatClient,
    id: "my-agent",
    name: "My Console Agent",
    description: "An agent for testing",
    tools: null  // or list of AITools
);

// 3. (Optional) Wrap in builder for pipeline
var builder = new AIAgentBuilder(agent);
var finalAgent = builder.Build();

// 4. Create session for state
var session = new ChatClientAgentSession();

// 5. Run agent
var response = await agent.RunAsync(
    "What is 2+2?",
    session: session,
    options: new ChatClientAgentRunOptions(),
    cancellationToken: CancellationToken.None
);

// 6. Get messages from response
foreach (var msg in response.Messages)
{
    Console.WriteLine($"{msg.Role}: {msg.Content}");
}
```

### Streaming:

```csharp
await foreach (var update in agent.RunStreamingAsync(
    "What is 2+2?",
    session: session,
    options: new ChatClientAgentRunOptions(),
    cancellationToken: CancellationToken.None))
{
    Console.WriteLine($"Update: {update}");
}
```

### With Tool Calling:

```csharp
// 1. Create tool
var addTool = AIFunctionFactory.Create(
    (int a, int b) => a + b,
    name: "Add",
    description: "Add two numbers"
);

// 2. Create ChatOptions with tools
var chatOptions = new ChatOptions
{
    Tools = new[] { new AITool { Function = addTool } },
    ToolMode = ChatToolMode.Auto  // Auto-invoke tools
};

// 3. Create agent
var agent = new ChatClientAgent(chatClient);

// 4. Run with tools
var response = await agent.RunAsync(
    "Add 5 and 3",
    session: session,
    options: new ChatClientAgentRunOptions(chatOptions: chatOptions)
);
```

